{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"[{\"title\":\"Departure x and x Friends\",\"number\":1,\"airDate\":\"2011-10-02\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The story begins with a young boy named Gon, who aspires to be a hunter just like his father Ging. Ging leaves his son in the care of Mito, Gon's aunt, and has not been seen since. Gon catches the local monster fish, \\\"Lord of the Lake\\\", in order to prove his ability to take the exam. Although Mito is reluctant to let Gon leave his home, she relents after he is determined to understand the reason his father left him and his interest of being a hunter.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4180539.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"タビダチ×ト×ナカマタチ\"},{\"title\":\"Test x of x Tests\",\"number\":2,\"airDate\":\"2011-10-09\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon, Kurapika and Leorio reach Dolle Harbor and are given instructions by the captain to head for the cedar tree on the hilltop behind the city. Moving through a small town, the three are stopped by a group of people, where an old woman gives a question requring them to choose from two choices. Answering wrongly, refusing to answer or attempting to head back will result in failure of the exam.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4181834.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"シケン×ノ×シケン\"},{\"title\":\"Rivals x for x Survival\",\"number\":3,\"airDate\":\"2011-10-16\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"With the navigators' help, Gon, Kurapika and Leorio arrive at Zaban City, the venue of the exam. The navigator leads them to a small restaurant, which is revealed to be the front for the venue. Gon's group is led to an elevator disguised as a back room, which leads a hundred floors underground. Below, they meet the rest of the participants and given their numbers. There they meet Tonpa, a regular participant who claims to have tried and failed 35 times in the exam.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4188272.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ライバル×ガ×サバイバル\"},{\"title\":\"Hope x and x Ambition\",\"number\":4,\"airDate\":\"2011-10-23\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"During the first test, a number of participants fall out from fatigue after running for at least forty kilometers. Leorio almost gives up until he is encouraged by Gon, who waits for him. Killua, a participant, is introduced and he is curious of Gon's personality when he discovers that the boy is the same age as him. Kurapika and Leorio talk about the reason for being a hunter, with Kurapika wanting to take down the Phantom Troupe as his clan was massacred by them for their precious scarlet eyes, which manifest when the Kurta uses their heightened sense. Leorio aims to be a hunter for money, for purely altruistic reasons, as his childhood friend died of an illness without the funds to save him. He wishes to be a doctor so he can give his patients free treatment. Finally, the participants reach the end of the tunnel they are in and up to the surface to the Numere Wetlands, also known as Swindlers' Swamp. Satotz warns them about the creatures using devious tactics to lure and eat their prey in the wetlands, and falling for their tricks equals death. A man claiming to be their original examiner says Satotz is a man-faced ape masquerading as their examiner to fool them. Hisoka, in the belief that a well-trained Hunter would be able to avoid attacks, throws his playing cards on Satotz and the man. The man is killed while Satotz stops the attack, revealing himself to be the real examiner. Hisoka is warned not to attack Satotz again otherwise he will be disqualified. Satotz tells the participants to follow him into the swamp, and if any of them loses sight of him, they will never reach the second venue.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4188248.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"キボウ×ト×ヤボウ\"},{\"title\":\"Hisoka x Is x Sneaky\",\"number\":5,\"airDate\":\"2011-10-30\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"While following Satotz, a fog moves into the swamp and most of the participants are either rendered unconscious or killed by traps and verocious beasts. A group of candidates target Hisoka as they feel he's a threat. Gon and Killua are separated from Leorio and Kurapika and both sides are eventually attacked by monsters. Leorio and Kurapika encounter Hisoka about to be attacked by candidates but are shocked to watch the magician easily take the candidates down. Hisoka then targets Leorio and Kurapika, but realizing that they are no match for him, they decide to head in different directions to stop him from following. However, Leorio returns, unable to run away from a fight. As expected, Leorio is beaten badly by Hisoka. Before the melee can get any worse, Gon, who is separated from Killua, arrives to stop Hisoka. Although he is also no match for Hisoka, he manages to hit his face once before being strangled by Hisoka.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4188249.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ヒソカ×ハ×ヒソカ\"},{\"title\":\"A x Surprising x Challenge\",\"number\":6,\"airDate\":\"2011-11-06\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon and Kurapika reunite with Leorio and Killua at the Phase Two site. Satotz leads what remains of the candidates to meet the second phase examiners, named Menchi and Buhara. The examiners declare the next phase is to test their cooking skills, much to the candidates' disbelief. The test requires pork, so the candidates are sent to find pigs in the forest. However, the pigs living inside the forest are carnivorous and tear through the candidates. Thanks to Gon, they discover the pigs' weakness and they manage to each get one for their cooking. Upon tasting the candidates' cooking, Buhara gives a pass but Menchi fails all of them. Knowing the candidates will riot, Satotz informs Chairman Netoros of the Hunter Selection Committee to make an appearance. Netoros arrives to correct Menchi's habit of getting biased whenever it's related to cooking. Netoros allows Menchi to stay on as examiner, and she gives the candidates a retest: boil eggs laid by spider eagles on Mt. Split-in-Half. The candidates ride on Netoros' airship to the mountain where they learn they have to jump down a potentially fatal height to get the eggs. Having seen and learnt how Menchi gets her egg, Gon leads some of the other candidates into successfully getting their own. Some candidates are killed while rashly trying to get their eggs while others refuse to take the leap. Out of the 50 candidates who survive to reach Phase Two, 42 candidates now remain.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4188250.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"イガイ×ナ×カダイ\"},{\"title\":\"Showdown x on the x Airship\",\"number\":7,\"airDate\":\"2011-11-13\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"All the candidates are told by Beans, Neteros' secretary to get their dinner and rest and prepare for the third phase the next morning. Tonpa tries to commit sabotage again by trying to keep Kurapika and Leorio awake for the whole night, but is exasperated to find that none of them fall for his tricks. Gon and Killua explore the airship, and Killua tells Gon that he is actually from a family of assassins. He wished to strike out on his own, which his family has not taken lightly. Neteros arrives and tests both boys' instinct and asks how they felt about the difficulty of the exam. Neteros invites both of them to a game, whoever can grab the ball he is holding before dawn will immediately pass the exam. Gon and Killua find it too hard to pass up, but discovers that with Neteros' skills, they are unable to grab the ball. Eventually Killua realizes that with their skills, they will never be able to take the ball from Neteros for a year, if he keeps it up. Killua retires, but then takes it out on two candidates who harass him, by maiming and killing them. Gon continues trying to grab the ball, and uses a headbutt on Neteros. The old man realizes that Gon will crack his skull if he continues with his headbutt, so he uses his right hand to push Gon away from him. Gon then tells Neteros then he has managed to get him to use his right hand once, which he had not used from the start of the challenge. After his speech, Gon falls asleep from exhaustion.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4188251.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ヒコウセン×ノ×ケッセン\"},{\"title\":\"Decision x by x Majority?\",\"number\":8,\"airDate\":\"2011-11-20\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The airship reaches Trick Tower, the Phase Three site, which is a tall featureless pillar built on an equally high platform. The candidates are told that to pass Phase 3, they have to climb down from the top to the base of the tower. An experienced rock climber candidate tries to climb down but is eaten by some flying monsters. Later, Kurapika finds that more than half of the candidates have discovered hidden doors to go inside the tower, which Gon finds one as well. However, the catch is that there are many hidden doors, each one can be only used once and only one person can fit through a door, which means they have to split up. When they try out different doors, they realize that they end up in the same room. In the room, Gon's group are given instructions and special wristwatches for five of them to follow the majority, but they cannot proceed without a fifth member. Lippo, one of the Phase 3 examiners tells them this while explaining they have chosen the path of majority rule.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4188252.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"カイケツ×ハ×タスウケツ?\"},{\"title\":\"Beware x of x Prisoners\",\"number\":9,\"airDate\":\"2011-11-27\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Tonpa promptly gives up even before Bendot land a punch on him. Leorio is furious at what he has done but Tonpa tells them that his real plan is to sabotage rookies like them. Gon then faces Sedokan, who proposes a match to see whose candle burns the longest. Gon chooses the longer candle, unaware that it is oil-soaked, and his candle starts to burn faster midway. Seeing that his candle is not susceptible to strong winds, he puts it down and sprints towards Sedokan to blow his candle. The next match is between Kurapika and Majitani, who proposes a death match without weapons and and with the condition that one must die or surrender to finish the match. Majitani, who relies on scaring and intimidating his enemies to make them surrender, is easily defeated by Kurapika when he sees something in Majitani and makes him see red.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4188253.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"シュウジン×ニ×ゴヨウジン\"},{\"title\":\"Trick x to the x Trick\",\"number\":10,\"airDate\":\"2011-12-04\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"A female prisoner claim that Majitani is only unconscious, thus Kurapika's match has not been settled. Leorio, and even Killua cannot persuade Kurapika to finish the fight for the latter refuses to fight a person who has lost the will to fight. Frustrated, Leorio decides to use the majority rule as a way out of the difficulty but no one supports him. Elsewhere Hisoka is met by Togari, a former examiner whom Hisoka attacked and is now wanting revenge. Togari attacks with four crescent blades, only to be finished with one sweeping attack. Hisoka then becomes the first applicant to pass this phase. Meanwhile, the team suspects Majitani's real condition. The female prisoner challenges Leorio to have a betting game instead. Leorio agrees and bets ten hours that Majitani is alive, which he wins. Next, he bets twenty hours on Majitani feigning unconsciousness. To confirm, he brings Majitani to the edge of the platform and threatens to drop him. Seeing that, the prisoner changes her bet to forty hours on Majitani being conscious. When he is about to be dropped by Leorio, Majitani moves and admits defeat, putting the score at 2 - 1 in favor of Leorio's team. However, they only have 20 hours left to wager\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4188254.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ヒッカケ×ノ×キッカケ\"},{\"title\":\"Trouble x with the x Gamble\",\"number\":11,\"airDate\":\"2011-12-11\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"After winning the bet about Majitani, Leroute, as what the prisoner is named, bets with Leorio about her gender. Despite looking conspicuously female, Leorio, much to Killua and Kurapika's annoyance, bets that she is male. Leorio thinks that team wins if he is correct; and if he is wrong, he will be able to touch Leroute to confirm. Leorio is wrong and goes on to check Leroute. Leorio then challenges Leroute in rock, paper, scissors, and loses. Killua then faces the feared mass murderer Johness the Dissector. Killua rips Johness' heart in an instant and even have it covered in a piece of Johness' cloth. The latter pleads for his heart, and Killua returned it after he is dead. The team thus gathers three points and pass the trial, but they are forced to wait the 50 hours that Leorio has lost with his bets in a small room. Meanwhile, applicants Gittarackur and Hanzo become the second and third one to finish the third phase.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4188255.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ギャンブル×デ×トラブル\"},{\"title\":\"Last x Test of x Resolve\",\"number\":12,\"airDate\":\"2011-12-18\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The team stays inside a small room for fifty hours and keep themselves from getting bored. Then they spend the remaining time going to a series of traps and tricks. At the last room, they encountered two doors and are forced to either choose the long and hard path (45 hours) in which all of them may use or the shortcut (about 3 minutes) wherein two of them must be left behind. As disputes break out among them, Gon comes up with an ingenious idea of opening the long way and breaking through the wall to go to the shortcut so all five of them pass this phase.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4188256.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"サイゴ×ノ×カクゴ\"},{\"title\":\"Letter x from x Gon\",\"number\":13,\"airDate\":\"2011-12-25\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon decides to send a letter to his aunt Mito in order to inform her about the events that had happened during his journey. He started to narrate the story on the events starting from the preliminary Hunter exam to the point when he met Leorio, Kurapika, Killua and the other examinees.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4188257.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ゴンヨリ×ノ×タヨリ\"},{\"title\":\"Hit x the x Target\",\"number\":14,\"airDate\":\"2012-01-08\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon learns to master his accuracy with his pole to try and steal Hisoka's number plate.Finally mastering it,He decides to steal it when Hisoka is busy catching his Prey.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4225824.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ターゲット×ニ×ヒット\"},{\"title\":\"Explosion x of x Deception\",\"number\":15,\"airDate\":\"2012-01-15\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon is relying on Bloodcrazy Butterflies to find his target, Hisoka, before waiting for the perfect time to use his skill with the fishing rod to snatch Hisoka's tag. Meanwhile, Leorio is tricked by Tonpa and loses his own tag, but Kurapika helps him recover it. Now that Kurapika and Leorio know that neither is the other's target, they decided to form an alliance.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4229917.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ダマシアイ×ノ×トリアイ\"},{\"title\":\"Defeat x and x Disgrace\",\"number\":16,\"airDate\":\"2012-01-22\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Kurapika and Leorio are being stalked by Hisoka, but they managed to negotiate their way out of a fight. However, the encounter leaves Hisoka aroused, so he leaves in search of a new target. Gon is able to use his fishing rod to snatch Hisoka's tag right when Hisoka attacks his target. However, as Gon tries to escape, he is attacked by another applicant and loses his tag...\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4229916.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ハイボク×ト×クツジョク\"},{\"title\":\"Trap x in the x Hole\",\"number\":17,\"airDate\":\"2012-01-29\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Killua grows tired of having Imori shadowing him so he challenges Imori to a fight and quickly dispatches him. Meanwhile, Gon has joined up with Leorio and Kurapika. The three of them devise a plan for taking Ponzu's tag and track her down to a suspicious-looking cave. That is when Leorio insists on heading in alone.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4229915.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"アナ×デ×ワナ\"},{\"title\":\"Big x Time x Interview\",\"number\":18,\"airDate\":\"2012-02-05\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon and his friends have been trapped inside a cave by poisonous snakes. Bourbon, the person responsible for the trap, is already dead, and nobody knows how to disarm the trap. Meanwhile, Leorio, who was bitten by the snakes, is growing weak. Gon manages to get them out of the sticky situation and through to the final phase of the exam. But first, Netero wants an interview with each of the remaining applicants...\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4229914.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"タイセツ×ナ×メンセツ\"},{\"title\":\"Can`t Win x and x Can`t Lose\",\"number\":19,\"airDate\":\"2012-02-12\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon and his friends have advanced to the final phase of the Hunter Exam. The final phase is a tournament where the winners are out and the losers advance. The rule is that if you kill your opponent, you'll be disqualified. The first mach is Gon versus Hanzo. Gon can't do anything against Hanzo, but he refuses to give up. Hanzo is losing his patience and threatens to break Gon's arm.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4229913.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"カテナイ×ガ×マケナイ\"},{\"title\":\"Baffling x Turn of x Events\",\"number\":20,\"airDate\":\"2012-02-19\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon wakes up, and finds himself being congratulated by Satotz for being the first person to pass the Hunter Exam. Gon asks Satotz if the Exam was still going on, and Satotz tells him that it's over. Satotz reveals what happens after he lost consciousness, and Gon finds out some shocking turn of events.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4229912.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"フカカイ×ナ×テンカイ\"},{\"title\":\"Some x Brother x Trouble\",\"number\":21,\"airDate\":\"2012-03-04\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon is upset that Killua was forced to kill. Gon is mad at Illumi and proclaims that he will go to Kukuroo Mountain to rescue Killua. As Gon and his friends depart, Satotz mentions that the Hunter Exam isn't over yet...\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4229911.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"キョウダイ×ノ×モンダイ\"},{\"title\":\"A x Dangerous x Watchdog\",\"number\":22,\"airDate\":\"2012-03-11\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon, Kurapica, and Leorio arrive at Kukuroo Mountain only to find out that they cannot get close to the Zoldyck family estate. The Zoldyck family owns the mountain and all of the surrounding forest and the entire region is gated shut. There is a guard outpost immediately outside of the gate, but instead of serving as a guard, the man working in there actually cleans up the mess created by the watchdog whenever there are intruders into the grounds. Gon, unwilling to give up on \\\"rescuing\\\" Killua, learns from the gatekeeper that the actual door is the massive stone gate and anyone who enters via that path will not be attacked by the watchdog. Leorio tries to pull and push on the gate, to no avail. The gatekeeper informs them that the gate opens up different amounts of stone slabs based only on the strength of the person; however, the least amount of strength anyone needs to open the smallest portion of the door requires two tons of strength on each side. In addition, the protagonists are shocked to hear that Killua opened up three doors, making the gate 16 tons, when he arrived home not long ago. Gon's naturally candid character that allows so many people to like him and to help him out will also play a role in how this episode plays out.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4229910.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"キケン×ナ×バンケン\"},{\"title\":\"The x Guard`s x Duty\",\"number\":23,\"airDate\":\"2012-03-18\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon and his friends have decided to pass through the Trial Gate to see Killua. First, they must train in the servants' residence until they can open the gate. Meanwhile, Killua has learned that Gon and the others are here to see him. Gon, Leorio, and Kurapika are able to open the gate after completing their training, but the apprentice butler Canary stands in their way.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4229909.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"バンニン×ノ×セキニン\"},{\"title\":\"The x Zoldyck x Family\",\"number\":24,\"airDate\":\"2012-03-25\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"With help from Canary, who is concerned about Killua, Gon and his friends are getting closer to the mansion. However, Kikyo tells them that Killua cannot see them as he is in solitary confinement. Meanwhile, Killua has been summoned by Silva and asked if he wants to see his friend? Killua answers truthfully, and he is allowed to go see his friends...\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4229908.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ゾルディック×ノ×カゾク\"},{\"title\":\"Can`t See x If x You`re Blind!\",\"number\":25,\"airDate\":\"2012-04-01\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon, Kurapika and Leorio arrive at the Butler's Quarters, where the Head Butler entertains them while waiting for Killua. But just what game does he have in mind, and what are the stakes?\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4229907.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ミエナイ×ト×アエナイ\"},{\"title\":\"Then x and x After\",\"number\":26,\"airDate\":\"2012-04-08\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"A letter from Gon arrives at Whale Island for Mito... (A recap of everything that has happened.)\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4292703.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"アレカラ×ト×ソレカラ\"},{\"title\":\"Arrival x at the x Arena\",\"number\":27,\"airDate\":\"2012-04-15\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon and Killua arrive at the Heavens Arena and begin to work their way up, making a new friend, Zushi, who is trained in the martial arts.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4298326.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"トウギジョウ×ニ×トウジョウ\"},{\"title\":\"Nen x and x Nen\",\"number\":28,\"airDate\":\"2012-04-22\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"While working to understand Nen and Ren, Gon and Killua run into a familiar acquaintance.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4298325.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ネン×ト×ネン\"},{\"title\":\"Awakening x and x Potential\",\"number\":29,\"airDate\":\"2012-04-29\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"After reaching the 200th floor, Gon and Killua run into Hisoka's barrier of Nen. They ask Wing to use the violent method for activating their Nen potential. As the deadline for registration draws near, they begin training in one of the four major principles of Nen, Ten.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4298324.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"カクセイ×ト×カノウセイ\"},{\"title\":\"Fierce x and x Ferocious\",\"number\":30,\"airDate\":\"2012-05-06\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon faces the Nen user Gido in his first 200s Heavens Arena match. Gon uses Ten to protect himself, but he soon finds himself on the defense against Gido's Dancing Tops. As Gon desperately tries to find a way to fight back, he makes a bold decision...\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4298323.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ゲキトウ×ト×カットウ\"},{\"title\":\"Destiny x and x Tenacity\",\"number\":31,\"airDate\":\"2012-05-13\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"A month has passed since Gon was seriously injured, and Hisoka and Kastro are about to fight in Heavens Arena. Kastro was able to knock Hisoka down in the past and sounds very confident in his interview. Hisoka appears unperturbed by the upcoming fight.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4298322.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"インネン×ト×シュウネン\"},{\"title\":\"A x Surprising x Win\",\"number\":32,\"airDate\":\"2012-05-20\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Kastro has used his ability to create a clone of himself with Nen to sever Hisoka's arm and take an advantage in the fight. However, despite losing both arms, Hisoka appears to be perfectly calm. Kastro loses his cool and attacks Hisoka.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4298321.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ドッキリ×ナ×ショウリ\"},{\"title\":\"An x Empty x Threat\",\"number\":33,\"airDate\":\"2012-05-27\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"After two months, Gon and Killua are finally allowed to practice Nen again. That's when Gido, Sadaso, and Riehlvelt appear before them and tell them to fight them in the arena. Gon and Killua refuse, but Killua finds Sadaso's behavior to be very suspicious.\\r\\n\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4298320.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ケイハク×ナ×キョウハク\"},{\"title\":\"Power x to x Avenge\",\"number\":34,\"airDate\":\"2012-06-03\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon has fights against Gido and Riehlvelt coming up. He's still mad about what they did to Zushi. Gon is able to withstand Gido's attacks and overwhelm him in battle. This causes Hisoka to smile.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4298319.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ジツリョク×デ×セツジョク\"},{\"title\":\"The x True x Pass\",\"number\":35,\"airDate\":\"2012-06-17\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon and Killua begin training in Hatsu, the culmination of everything they've learned about Nen. And finally, Gon challenges Hisoka to return the favor from the Hunter Exam. \\\"I'm going to give the tag back to Hisoka while punching him in the face!\\\"\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4298318.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"セイカク×ナ×ゴウカク\"},{\"title\":\"A Big Debt x and x a Small Kick\",\"number\":36,\"airDate\":\"2012-06-24\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"After landing a punch on Hisoka, Gon returns the tag from the Hunter Exam. Hisoka is ecstatic to see Gon's development and uses his own Nen to attack. Gon is scared, but he recklessly continues to attack! Will he emerge victorious.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4298317.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"オオキナカリ×ト×チイサナケリ\"},{\"title\":\"Ging x and x Gon\",\"number\":37,\"airDate\":\"2012-07-01\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"After learning Nen and becoming a true Hunter, Gon returns to Whale Island with Killua. When he arrives, Mito has a box for him. She was told by Ging to give this box to Gon once he became a Hunter. However, it appears that the box cannot be opened.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4298316.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ジン×ト×ゴン\"},{\"title\":\"Reply x from x Dad\",\"number\":38,\"airDate\":\"2012-07-08\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon and Killua have begun to listen to the cassette tape left behind by Ging in anticipation of Gon becoming a Hunter. What remains in this foretelling message from Gon's long-absent father?\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4341414.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"オヤジ×ノ×ヘンジ\"},{\"title\":\"Wish x and x Promise\",\"number\":39,\"airDate\":\"2012-07-15\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Having learned his Nen ability, Kurapika pursues a Hunter's work that will get him close to the New York auction.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4341415.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ネガイ×ト×チカイ\"},{\"title\":\"Nen x Users x Unite?\",\"number\":40,\"airDate\":\"2012-07-22\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Kurapika and the other job candidates have to battle their way out of the employers mansion... if they ever hope of obtaining any of the items they even need for the job.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4341416.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ノウリョクシャ×ハ×キョウリョクシャ?\"},{\"title\":\"Gathering x of x Heroes\",\"number\":41,\"airDate\":\"2012-07-29\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The biggest auction in the world is about to take place in York New City. The Phantom Troupe leader, Chrollo, has instructed the members to gather in the city. For what purpose? The band of murdering thieves is about to make its move.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4354712.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ゴウケツ×ノ×シュウケツ\"},{\"title\":\"Defend x and x Attack\",\"number\":42,\"airDate\":\"2012-08-05\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The auction is finally about to begin. Gon, Killua, and Leorio are working hard to amass enough money to buy Greed Island. Kurapika has been assigned to monitor the auction house. Meanwhile, the Phantom Troupe draws close. All paths will soon cross in York New City.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4354696.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"マモル×ト×セメル\"},{\"title\":\"A x Shocking x Tragedy\",\"number\":43,\"airDate\":\"2012-08-12\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The Phantom Troupe attacks the underground auction held by the Mafia. Afterwards, there is no sign of the merchandise or guests. The Mafia place a reward on their heads and begin pursuit. Kurapika and the other bodyguards on patrol join the pursuit. Kurapika is drawing closer to the Phantom Troupe.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4354697.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ショウゲキ×ノ×サンゲキ\"},{\"title\":\"Buildup x to a x Fierce Battle\",\"number\":44,\"airDate\":\"2012-08-19\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"After Uvogin slaughters the Mafia's pursuit, the Mafia dispatches their secret weapon, the Shadow Beasts. However, Uvogin is able to defeat them by himself. During the battle, the spider tattoo on Uvogin's back is revealed, and Kurapika springs to action.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4354698.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ゲキセン×ノ×フクセン\"},{\"title\":\"Restraint x and x Vow\",\"number\":45,\"airDate\":\"2012-09-02\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Kurapika was able to capture Uvogin, a member of the Phantom Troupe. Kurapika struggles to control his rage as Uvogin makes demands as though he isn't a captive. That is when Kurapika receives an e-mail from Hisoka...\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4354699.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"コウソク×ト×ヤクソク\"},{\"title\":\"Chasing x and x Waiting\",\"number\":46,\"airDate\":\"2012-09-09\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Uvogin was able to escape with some help from his fellow bandits. However, after the blow to his pride, he is determined to track down and Kurapika and defeat him. Kurapika realizes that the Phantom Troupe has identified their location and moves the boss to a safe place while awaiting the Phantom Troupe's arrival by himself.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4354700.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"オウモノ×ト×マツモノ\"},{\"title\":\"Condition x and x Condition\",\"number\":47,\"airDate\":\"2012-09-16\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The anticipated battle between Kurapika and Uvogin begins! Can Kurapika really withstand Uvogin's abilities, and just what are the full extent of the powers in Kurapika's chains?\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4354701.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"セイヤク×ト×セイヤク\"},{\"title\":\"Very x Sharp x Eye\",\"number\":48,\"airDate\":\"2012-09-23\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon, Killua, and Leorio are trying to get their hands on enough money to buy Greed Island. As they pass through the market, Gon stumbles across a way to identify valuable items. The plan is to buy cheap and sell low, but someone else is bidding on all their items.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4354703.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"メキキ×ノ×キキメ\"},{\"title\":\"Pursuit x and x Analysis\",\"number\":49,\"airDate\":\"2012-09-30\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon and his friends are hoping to win the reward that's been placed on the Phantom Troupe. At the same time, Machi and Nobunaga have been dispatched to search for the \\\"chain user\\\" because Uvogin hasn't returned. Gon and Killua receive a tip and begin shadowing the two Troupe members.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4354704.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ツイセキ×デ×ブンセキ\"},{\"title\":\"Ally x and x Sword\",\"number\":50,\"airDate\":\"2012-10-07\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon and Killua have been captured by the Phantom Troupe. They are questioned about the chain user that the Troupe is searching for, but the two of them don't know that the chain user is Kurapika. As they're about to be released, Nobunaga decides to keep them around as potential recruits for the Troupe. Will Gon and Killua be able to escape?\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4354705.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ナカマ×ト×カタナ\"},{\"title\":\"A x Brutal x Battlefield\",\"number\":51,\"airDate\":\"2012-10-14\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The auction has been rescheduled, and the Mafia expects the Phantom Troupe to attack again. The Ten Dons have hired multiple assassins to deal with the Phantom Troupe. Light Nostrade sends Kurapika to join the assassins in dispatching of the Troupe.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4414964.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ヒジョウ×ノ×センジョウ\"},{\"title\":\"Assault x and x Impact\",\"number\":52,\"airDate\":\"2012-10-21\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The Troupe is attacking the auction with all their power. The Ten Dons hired assassins are no match, except for Zeno and Silva. \\r\\n\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4417609.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"シュウゲキ×ト×ショウゲキ\"},{\"title\":\"Fake x and x Psyche\",\"number\":53,\"airDate\":\"2012-10-28\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The leader of the Phantom Troupe is dead... Kurapika is shocked by the news. Unconvinced, he tries to get a glimpse of the body. Meanwhile, the dead bodies of the other Troupe members have been discovered.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4420731.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"フェイク×デ×サイク\"},{\"title\":\"Fortunes x Aren`t x Right?\",\"number\":54,\"airDate\":\"2012-11-04\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon, Killua, Kurapika, and Leorio are finally reunited. Kurapika reveals his Nen powers to the others. However, Killua is afraid that Kurapika is now in danger because one of the Troupe members can read minds. Meanwhile, Chrollo is using the fortune telling power he stole from Neon to tell the fortunes of the Troupe members.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4420732.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ウラナイ×ガ×アタラナイ?\"},{\"title\":\"Allies x and x Lies\",\"number\":55,\"airDate\":\"2012-11-11\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"After Chrollo tells fortunes for all of the Troupe members, they suspect that Hisoka has betrayed them. Hisoka's desire to fight Chrollo drives him to take a big risk by altering his own fortune. Meanwhile, after learning that the Troupe is still alive, Kurapika teams up with Gon and friends and work on a plan to capture Pakunoda.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4420733.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ナカマ×ト×イカサマ\"},{\"title\":\"Beloved x and x Beleaguered\",\"number\":56,\"airDate\":\"2012-11-18\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Chrollo uses the information he has on Neon to identify the location of the chain user, Kurapika. Meanwhile, Killua is keeping an eye on the Phantom Troupe base when he is joined by Melody, who helps determine that the Troupe is headed towards Kurapika's hotel. The Troupe is finally closing in on Kurapika.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4420734.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"サイアイ×ト×サイアク\"},{\"title\":\"Initiative x and x Law\",\"number\":57,\"airDate\":\"2012-12-02\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The Phantom Troupe has learned that Kurapika was the one who killed Uvogin. It's only a matter of time before they realize that the captured Gon and Killua are working with Kurapika? Chrollo takes Gon and killua to the hotel lobby, where Paknoda and the other Troupe members are waiting. Suddenly, the lights go out. Gon and Killua try to escape in the darkness. But Chrollo is the one who has vanished...\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4420735.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"センテ×ト×オキテ\"},{\"title\":\"Signal x to x Retreat\",\"number\":58,\"airDate\":\"2012-12-09\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Kurapika has captured Chrollo. He offers to release Chrollo if Pakunoda brings Gon and Killua to him. However, Kurapika is unable to control his emotions in the presence of the Troupe leader. Will Kurapika finally have his revenge?\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4420736.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ヒキギワ×ノ×ヒキガネ\"},{\"title\":\"Bid x and x Haste\",\"number\":59,\"airDate\":\"2014-02-19\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Cheetu attempts to provoke Zeno into fighting him, but Silva appears to pick up his father, killing the ant instanly in the occasion. Separated from the others, Youpi realizes that he failed to prevent the intruders from approaching the king and attempts to vent out his anger on Knuckle and Shoot, creating an overwhelming explosion, a feat that surprised even himself. Knuckle believes this could prove itself as an opportunity to make a comeback, while Youpi plans to use it to defeat them for good.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4798644.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"セリ×ト×アセリ\"},{\"title\":\"End x and x Beginning\",\"number\":60,\"airDate\":\"2014-02-26\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Ikalgo infiltrates the palace's lower levels to look for Palm with no success. While returning to the surface, his cover is blown and he finds himself trapped in the undergound with an enemy. Meanwhile, Youpi pretends to be angered in order to have Knuckle falsely believe there is an opening for him to attack. Youpi's plan works, but just before he could kill his opponent, Killua paralyzes the ant with a lighting bolt and steps in to fight him.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4803027.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"キマリ×ト×ハジマリ\"},{\"title\":\"Invitation x and x Friend\",\"number\":61,\"airDate\":\"2014-03-05\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Taking advantage of Youpi's distraction, Killua vents out his anger by beating him up, but is forced to flee after his lighting power runs out. Meanwhile, Ikalgo makes use of the underground security system to outsmart his pursuer and find a way to escape back to surface. Morel, on the other hand, is in doubt about whether he should make the first move against Pouf or not.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4805438.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"カンユウ×ト×シンユウ\"},{\"title\":\"Reality x and x Raw\",\"number\":62,\"airDate\":\"2014-03-12\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Morel decides to make the first move and unwillingly frees Pouf from his restrain. Upon realizing that Shoot is missing, unaware that he was taken by Knov to be treated, Knuckle confronts Youpi, assisted by Morel, whose options are drastically reduced upon having his pipe stolen by Pouf, who after realizing that the king is nowhere to be found, decides to rejoin Pitou, who is still working to stabilize Komugi under Gon's vigilant eyes.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4805439.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ゲンジツ?×ト×ゲンセキ\"},{\"title\":\"A x Hard x Master\",\"number\":63,\"airDate\":\"2014-03-19\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Knuckle and Morel confront Youpi with their lives on the line, but just a few moments left of neutralizing his nen with his ability, he is forced to abandon his master or give up on defeating his oponent.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4805440.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"シショウ×ハ×ヒジョウ?\"},{\"title\":\"Strengthen x and x Threaten\",\"number\":64,\"airDate\":\"2014-03-26\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Far away from the palace, Netero prepares himself to confront the king, who much to his surprise, recognizes his value as a fighter and is not willing to kill him. Meanwhile, Pouf learns the situation from Pitou and sneaks past Gon's vigilance to rejoin Youpi as they leave the palace to search for the king.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4805441.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"キョウカ×ト×キョウカツ\"},{\"title\":\"Evil Fist x and x Rock-Paper-Scissors\",\"number\":65,\"airDate\":\"2014-04-02\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Ikalgo is attacked by Welfin but the enemy's attempt to restrain him backfires and they find themselves in a stand off. In the occasion, Welfin regains some of his lost memories from when he was still human and gives him a hint regarding Palm's location.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4839884.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ジャケン×ト×ジャンケン\"},{\"title\":\"Strategy x and x Scheme\",\"number\":66,\"airDate\":\"2014-04-09\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Killua meets Palm and learns that she was transformed into a Chimera. Refusing to let her see Gon in fear of what effects this could have on his already unstable mind, Killua is attacked by her, unaware that she is under Pouf's control.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4839887.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"コウリャク×ト×サクリャク\"},{\"title\":\"15 x 15\",\"number\":67,\"airDate\":\"2014-04-16\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Netero convinces the king to fight him by revealing that he will tell him his true name once defeated. The chairman then unleashes his most powerful technique that despite striking the king countless times, only manages to scratch him.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4839888.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"15×ト×15\"},{\"title\":\"Pirates x and x Guesses\",\"number\":68,\"airDate\":\"2014-04-23\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The fight between Netero and the king comes to an end\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4839889.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"カイゾク×ト×スイソク\"},{\"title\":\"A x Heated x Showdown\",\"number\":69,\"airDate\":\"2014-04-30\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Pitou completes Komugi's treatment and Gon forces her to accompany him to Peijing in order to restore Kaito's mind, while Komugi stays behind with Killua and the others. Meanwhile, Pouf and Youpi reach the site of Netero's battle with Meruem and can't hide their feelings of sadness upon finding their king's maimed body.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4839890.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"タイケツ×デ×ネッケツ\"},{\"title\":\"Guts x and x Courage\",\"number\":70,\"airDate\":\"2014-05-07\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Pouf and Youpi sacrifice most of their own bodies to heal Meruem, who rises stronger than before, but with most of his memories missing. Pouf then decides to take this opportunity to dispose of Komugi in hopes that Meruem never remembers about her at all, but is attacked by the other hunters, who realize, much to their horror, that the king is still alive and is about to return to the palace.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4870970.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"コンジョウ×ト×ユウジョウ\"},{\"title\":\"Bargain x and x Deal\",\"number\":71,\"airDate\":\"2014-05-14\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Shaiapouf's plan to kill Komugi is thwarted when Killua faces him in a battle of words and speed. When the King arrives in the palace, Shaiapouf is resolved to get rid of the Gungi board before the King can remember anything else. Finally, Neferpitou and Gon arrive at the place of their long-awaited battle.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4876781.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"カケヒキ×ト×トリヒキ\"},{\"title\":\"Chase x and x Chance\",\"number\":72,\"airDate\":\"2014-05-21\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Shaiapouf continues his plan to remove anything that could trigger Meruem's memory of Komugi as the King arrives at the palace. Killua continues to hold onto Komugi, and meets with Palm. Gon and Neferpitou arrive where Kite is, however, Gon must now face the truth.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4884760.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"チェイス×デ×チャンス\"},{\"title\":\"Insanity x and x Sanity\",\"number\":73,\"airDate\":\"2014-05-28\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"After telling gon the truth about Kite, Pitou tells gon that she is sorry for what she did, but it's too late for apologies.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4888651.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"キョウキ×ト×ショウキ\"},{\"title\":\"Victor x and x Loser\",\"number\":74,\"airDate\":\"2014-06-04\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The King still struggles to retrieve his memories as he and his two remaining Royal Guards return to the palace. He eventually knocks out Meleoron and Knuckle Bine with his En, and later engages Shaiapouf and Menthuthuyoupi in a race against time. Meanwhile, only two remain, Palm and Ikalgo, and hide an unconscious Komugi underground.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4893739.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ショウシャ×ト×ハイシャ\"},{\"title\":\"Ging`s Friends x and x True Friends\",\"number\":75,\"airDate\":\"2014-06-11\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"A message of hostage exchange sends Welfin on the field. One moment he encounters Menthuthuyoupi, and the next, Shaiapouf finds Youpi lifeless. When he returns to the King, Meruem demands Shaiapouf's secrets. On their way, Shaiapouf unsuspectingly coughs out blood, just like how blood trickled from the King and Menthuthuyoupi.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4900249.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ジンノトモ×ト×シンノトモ\"},{\"title\":\"Reunion x and x Understanding\",\"number\":76,\"airDate\":\"2014-06-18\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Meruem uses his final permissible En and enlightens his surrounding with that and approaches to Welfin who was not detected by his En earlier. Caught between the desire to live and avoidable death, Welfin finally utters the name of Komugi and the secret Shaiapouf was trying so hard to protect now is finally revealed with Meruem regaining all of his memories about Komugi.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4905356.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"サイカイ×ト×リカイ\"},{\"title\":\"Unease x and x Sighting\",\"number\":77,\"airDate\":\"2014-06-25\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Now knowing his fate, Meruem admits defeat and reveals that all he wants now is to spend his final moments playing with Komugi, convincing Palm to tell him where she is hidden. East Gorteau and the NGL gets in turmoil after the fall of the Chimera Ants and the Hunter Association start making preparations to decide who will succeed Netero as its president. Despite knowing that she will also be poisoned to death by staying close to Meruem, Komugi stays by his side until his last breath and passes away in sequence.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4910983.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"フアン×ト×シュツゲン\"},{\"title\":\"Very x Rapid x Reproduction\",\"number\":78,\"airDate\":\"2014-07-02\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"After the fall of the king, the remaining Chimera Ants move on with their lives, each following their own path. However, Gon is still in critical condition after his battle with Neferpitou and Killua departs in search for a way to heal his body. Meanwhile, the top members of the Hunter Association, the Zodiacs, assemble to organize the election to choose the next president, following the will of Netero's last message.\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/252322/4917135.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"キュウソク×ナ×ゾウショク\"},{\"title\":\"No x Good x NGL\",\"number\":79,\"airDate\":\"2013-05-12\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"After passing a strict border checkpoint, Gon and his new friends enter NGL where they suspect the Chimera Ant is.  However, ten other teams of Hunters have already arrived before them.  Meanwhile, the Chimera Ants, with their new names and individual personalities, are attacking humans.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170251/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"NG×ナ×NGL\"},{\"title\":\"Evil x and x Terrible\",\"number\":80,\"airDate\":\"2013-05-19\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Pokkle and Ponzu use Ponzu`s bees to deliver messages asking the Hunter Association to help eliminate the Chimera Ants.  Meanwhile, the Chimera Ants have attacked Gyro, the shadowy ruler of NGL, and taken his guns.  As the situation gets worse, Ponzu`s message reaches Gon`s group\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170252/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ゴクアク×ト×サイアク\"},{\"title\":\"The x Fight x Begins\",\"number\":81,\"airDate\":\"2013-05-26\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon, Killua, and Kite discover the remains of a destroyed village.  There, they encounter their first Chimera Ant.  Gon and Killua are shaken by the speed and power displayed by the Chimera Ant.  However, Kite tells them that they must defeat the Chimera Ant or leave.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170253/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"タタカイ×ノ×カイシ\"},{\"title\":\"Kite x and x Slots\",\"number\":82,\"airDate\":\"2013-06-02\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Some of the more aggressive Chimera Ants have eaten the villains who ran the NGL underground and grown increasingly evil.  When Gon looks away from their gruesome act, Kite admonishes him.  Now, they must battle for their lives.  Meanwhile, a Chimera Ant is on the verge of discovering Nen.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170254/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"カイト×ノ×スロット\"},{\"title\":\"Inspiration x to x Evolve\",\"number\":83,\"airDate\":\"2013-06-09\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The Hunter Association has dispatched an expeditionary force to exterminate the Chimera Ants.  Meanwhile, Gon and his friends are being targeted by Chimera Ants who seek to eat rare humans.  They are forced into one-on-one battles with Chimera Ant captains.  They easily dispatch their opponents, but Kite continues to feel uneasy.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170255/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"カンカ×シテ×シンカ\"},{\"title\":\"A x Fated x Awakening\",\"number\":84,\"airDate\":\"2013-06-16\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Hagya sends his soldiers after Gon, Killua, and Kite in an attempt to capture rare humans.  Gon and his friends struggle to find inside the forest as Chimera Ants relentlessly attack.  At the same time, one of the Queen`s Royal Guards has been born.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170256/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"サダメ×ノ×メザメ\"},{\"title\":\"Light x and x Darkness\",\"number\":85,\"airDate\":\"2013-06-23\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Kite, Gon, and Killua follow Hagya as they seek the Chimera Ant nest where the Queen awaits.  However, as they are about to reach the Queen`s castle, one of the Royal Guards, Pitou, appears before them.  Pitou attacks Kite with ferocious speed.  How do Gon and Killua react?\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170257/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ヒカリ×ト×カゲ\"},{\"title\":\"Promise x and x Reunion\",\"number\":86,\"airDate\":\"2013-06-30\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Kite used himself as a decoy to allow Gon and Killua to escape.  The two boys vow to save Kite, believing that he lives.  However, to return to NGL, they must clear the condition set by Chairman Netero, leader of the expeditionary force, which is to defeat two assassins and take their tokens.  Gon and Killua accept the condition and return to the board by the train station.  That is when they sense an ominous aura behind the.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170258/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"チカイ×ト×サイカイ\"},{\"title\":\"Duel x and x Escape\",\"number\":87,\"airDate\":\"2013-07-07\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon and Killua are training to take the tokens from their targets.  Immediately after finishing their training, they`re sent exhausted by Bisky to fight Knuckle.  Gon and Killua don`t feel very good about their chances to win.  Will they figure out a way to defeat the stronger Knuckle?\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170259/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ケットウ×シテ×トウソウ\"},{\"title\":\"Rock-Paper-Scissors x and x Weakness\",\"number\":88,\"airDate\":\"2013-07-14\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon and Killua head back to their lodging, exhausted after the battle with Knuckle.  That is when their second opponent, Shoot, attempts to finish them off.  However, he leaves in a cold sweat without making a move.  Palm is worried about the progress that Gon and Killua are making in their training, but Gon promises that they will win.  Meanwhile in the Queen`s castle, the growing King`s fetus begins to pulse.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170260/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ジャンケン×ト×ジャクテン\"},{\"title\":\"Compassion x and x Strength\",\"number\":89,\"airDate\":\"2013-07-21\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon has finally forced Knuckle to use his full strength.  However, Knuckle immediately identifies the weakness in Jajanken, Gon`s special attack.  Knuckle goes on the attack by exploiting those weaknesses.  Gon finds myself unable to fight back.  However, he continues to attempt to charge up his Nen for Jajanken.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170261/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ヤサシサ×ト×ツヨサ\"},{\"title\":\"Interest x and x Curse\",\"number\":90,\"airDate\":\"2013-07-28\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon and Killua are finally facing off against Knuckle and Shoot.  Killua takes Shoot while Gon`s opponent is Knuckle.  Gon succeeds in sensing Knuckle through his aura, but then LoanBoy pops up on his left arm.  Meanwhile, Killua is struggling against Shoot.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170262/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"リソク×ト×ジュバク\"},{\"title\":\"The Strong x and x the Weak\",\"number\":91,\"airDate\":\"2013-08-04\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"At long last, the Queen gives birth to the King.  The Chimera Ants are cowed by the menancing aura emitted by the King.  Pitou, Pouf, and Youpi kneel before the King to greet him, but with that gesture, they have abandoned the Queen.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170263/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"キョウシャ×ト×ジャクシャ\"},{\"title\":\"One Wish x and x Two Promises\",\"number\":92,\"airDate\":\"2013-08-11\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"After surrendering, Colt requests that the Hunters save the dying Queen.  Morel immediately dispatches a team of researchers to the castle.  Inside, Knuckle and Shoot discover an incredible sight.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170264/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ヒトツノネガイ×ト×フタツノチカイ\"},{\"title\":\"Date x with x Palm\",\"number\":93,\"airDate\":\"2013-08-18\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The King is on the move.  After invading the Republic of East Gorteau and eating a Nen user`s aura, his own power grows.  Meruem quickly takes control of the palace.  Meanwhile, after losing to Knuckle and Shoot, Gon and Killua return to the inn to face Palm`s wrath for breaking their promise to take her to NGL.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170265/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"パーム×ト×デート\"},{\"title\":\"Friend x and x Journey\",\"number\":94,\"airDate\":\"2013-09-01\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"While Gon is on a date with Palm, Killua, who was tailing them, encounters Rammot in the forest.  Killua does not want to let Gon, who can`t use Nen, get in a fight, so he takes on Rammot alone.  However, he cannot rid himself of his brother Illumi`s voice in his head that keeps telling him to run.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170266/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"トモダチ×ト×タビダチ\"},{\"title\":\"Grudge x and x Dread\",\"number\":95,\"airDate\":\"2013-09-08\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Knuckle and Morel face off against Cheetu. The difference in physical strength between Chimera Ants and humans is immense, as the two Hunters appear to be overwhelmed by Cheetu`s speed. However, Knuckle and Morel have a plan. Armed with wit and experience, they begin by having Morel cover the area with white smoke.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170267/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ウラミ×ト×スゴミ\"},{\"title\":\"A x Lawless x Home\",\"number\":96,\"airDate\":\"2013-09-15\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Meteor City, home of the Phantom Troupe.  Kalluto, Feitan, Shalnark, Phinks, Shizuku, and Bonolenov arrive after hearing that Chimera Ants have taken over.  Upon arriving, they come across grotesquely disfigured bodies.  It is the work of Zazan, who has built her nest atop the garbage of Meteor City.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170268/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ムホウ×ナ×ホーム\"},{\"title\":\"Carnage x and x Devastation\",\"number\":97,\"airDate\":\"2013-09-22\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Zazan has built a new Chimera Ant nest in Meteor City, home of the Phantom Troupe. The Phantom Troupe members head inside the nest to defeat Zazan. Inside, they split up to fight Zazan`s underlings. The Phantom Troupe reveal their secret abilities, but will it be enough to exterminate the Chimera Ants?\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170269/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ゲキトウ×デ×ゲキメツ\"},{\"title\":\"Infiltration x and x Selection\",\"number\":98,\"airDate\":\"2013-09-29\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon and Killua infiltrate the Republic of East Gorteau in an attempt to stop the selection process that is occurring. They arrive at a village, only to find it deserted. However, after discovering traces of blood on the floors and walls, they follow the trail outside to a mass grave that has been disturbed by wild dogs. Killua then realizes what the true purpose of the national celebration is.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170270/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"センニュウ×ト×センベツ\"},{\"title\":\"Combination x and x Evolution\",\"number\":99,\"airDate\":\"2013-10-09\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Killua and Gon split up to stop the selection process, but Gon finds his path blocked by two new Chimera ants, an owl and a bat. Both are nocturnal hunters. Gon has a hard time coping with how loud the bat`s wings are and how soft the owl`s wings are.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170271/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"コンビネーション×ト×エボリューション\"},{\"title\":\"Tracking x and x Pursuit\",\"number\":100,\"airDate\":\"2013-10-16\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Knuckle and Shoot attempt to ambush Cheetu, but at the last moment, Cheetu changes directions and vanishes. The two Hunters realize that someone must have warned Cheetu. Meanwhile, Killua and Gon are both being followed. The Chimera Ant following Gon decides to reveal himself.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170272/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ツイセキ×ニハ×ツイゲキ\"},{\"title\":\"Ikalgo x and x Lightning\",\"number\":101,\"airDate\":\"2013-10-23\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"After splitting up with Gon, Killua is attacked by an octopus Chimera Ant named Ikalgo. Ikalgo has the ability to possess humans and transform his legs into a cannon for firing projectiles. However, he`s captured by Killua before he can find a host. Killua tells Ikalgo that he`ll spare his life in return for information about his ally`s powers, but Ikalgo tells Killua that he won`t sell out.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170273/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"イカルゴ×ト×イカズチ\"},{\"title\":\"Power x and x Games\",\"number\":102,\"airDate\":\"2013-10-30\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Ikalgo betrays his fellow Chimera Ants to save Killua, his former enemy. At the same time, Gon is bonding with a Chimera Ant named Melereon. Melereon tells Gon about his own power, which is a risky move for a Nen user. However, he`s willing to take that risk to build a relationship of trust with Gon, for his objective is to defeat Meruem, the Chimera Ant King.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170274/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ノウリョク×ト×タイキョク\"},{\"title\":\"Check x and x Mate\",\"number\":103,\"airDate\":\"2013-11-06\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The King is finding ways to entertain himself while waiting for the selection. He summons masters of Shogi and Go and defeats them in matches. It appears that he has incredible physical and mental strength. Next, the King summons Komugi, a blind girl who is the world champion of a board game called Gungi which originated in the Republic of East Gorteau. When the match begins, the blind girl opens her eyes.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170275/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ツミ×ト×ヨミ\"},{\"title\":\"Doubt x and x Hesitation\",\"number\":104,\"airDate\":\"2013-11-13\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The Hunter Knov is making his way towards the Palace.  The Chimera Ants Leol and Flutter are watching Knov in an attempt to learn what powers he has, but they lose sight of him.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170276/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"マヨイ×ト×トマドイ\"},{\"title\":\"Resolve x and x Awakening\",\"number\":105,\"airDate\":\"2013-11-20\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The King`s meeting with world champion Gungi player Komugi has left him baffled and irritated. However, he`s also enjoying their matches.  The King proposes that they wager on their next match, promising Komugi that he will grant any wish she makes if she wins.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170277/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"カクゴ×ト×カクセイ\"},{\"title\":\"Knov x and x Morel\",\"number\":106,\"airDate\":\"2013-11-27\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"While the King and Komugi continue to play Gungi, Knov has successfully infiltrated the palace.  His objective is to play four-dimensional exits for the other Hunters to use.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170278/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ノヴ×ト×モラウ\"},{\"title\":\"Return x and x Retire\",\"number\":107,\"airDate\":\"2013-12-04\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The lion Chimera Ant Leol has chased Morel into an underground cathedral for a duel.  Leol activates his Nen ability to create large waves and a surfboard.  The waves are used to attack Morel while Leol rides the surfboard and charges Morel.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170279/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"リターン×ト×リタイヤ\"},{\"title\":\"Gungi x of x Komugi\",\"number\":108,\"airDate\":\"2013-12-11\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Three days remain until the selection begins. Gon and the other Hunters are joined by new allies as they prepare to infiltrate the palace. Meanwhile, King Mereum, who has recovered from his injury, and Komugi continue to play Gungi. However, Komugi has grown fatigued.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170280/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"コムギ×ノ×グンギ\"},{\"title\":\"Taking Stock x and x Taking Action\",\"number\":109,\"airDate\":\"2013-12-18\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Only one day remains before the selection begins. Gon, Killua, and Ikalgo go over the operation plan one more time. They attempt to simulate every possible scenario. Meanwhile, a siren begins to blare inside Peijing.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170281/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"コウシンカイシ×デ×コウドウカイシ\"},{\"title\":\"Confusion x and x Expectation\",\"number\":110,\"airDate\":\"2013-12-25\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The citizens of East Gorteau are assembling in front of the palace.Meanwhile, Welfin, a wolf Chimera Ant, has noticed that someone infiltrated the palace. At the same time, Secretary Bizeff has realized that Palm has disappeared and begins to search for her.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170282/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"コンワク×ト×オモワク\"},{\"title\":\"Charge x and x Invade\",\"number\":111,\"airDate\":\"2014-01-08\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"\\\"One minute to go.\\\"  Gon, Killua, Knuckle, Shoot, Melereon, and the others are waiting inside the Four-dimension Apartment.  Morel tells the Hunters to prepare for the attack.  Two minutes earlier, two glowing lights descended upon the Republic of East Gorteau.  Neferpitou was the first to notice them. \\\"Something`s coming.\\\"  A few seconds later, Neferpitou`s hunch was confirmed. \\\"The enemy!\\\" A giant dragon drops out of the clouds. The final battle pitting human against Chimera Ant is about to begin.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170283/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"トツニュウ×シテ×シンニュウ\"},{\"title\":\"Monster x and x Monster\",\"number\":112,\"airDate\":\"2014-01-15\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Zeno and Netero`s attack throws the palace into chaos. Gon, Killua, and Shoot encounter Youpi at the bottom of the stairway leading up to the King`s room.  Meanwhile, Pitou and Pouf rush to the King, fearing the worst.  Upon arrival, Pitou begins to shed tears.  What has happened to the King?\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170284/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"カイブツ×ト×カイブツ\"},{\"title\":\"An x Indebted x Insect\",\"number\":113,\"airDate\":\"2014-01-22\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"After Gon and the Hunters infiltrate the palace, they are separated by a powerful attack from Youpi. Morel uses his Nen smoke to distract Youpi and head towards the King, leaving Shoot and Knuckle to deal with the Royal Guard.  At the same time, Gon and Killua also spring into action.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170285/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ムシ×ダケド×カシ\"},{\"title\":\"Divide x and x Conquer\",\"number\":114,\"airDate\":\"2014-01-29\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Shaiapouf faces off against Morel while Menthuthuyoupi is up against Shoot and Knuckle.  As the various players begin their battles, the King, Netero, and Zeno also square off. Zeno uses his Nen ability Dragon Head on the King, but the King does not try to dodge.  What is the King`s objective?  The ultimate battle between the King and Netero is about to begin.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170286/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ブンダン×ト×ゴサン\"},{\"title\":\"Duty x and x Question\",\"number\":115,\"airDate\":\"2014-02-05\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Ikalgo is alone underground a mission to find Palm. Meanwhile, Knuckle has abandoned Meleron`s Perfect Plan and revealed himself to Youpi. Melereon leaves Knuckle and Shoot to assist the others. However, Welfin is sharp enough to notice that Flutter, under Ikalgo`s control, is behaving strangely. He also catches Melereon`s scent and gives pursuit.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170287/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ギム×ト×ギモン\"},{\"title\":\"Revenge x and x Recovery\",\"number\":116,\"airDate\":\"2014-02-12\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Killua now understands what Zeno meant when he said to draw their own conclusions about what was happening inside. Gon and Killua enter the tower where Neferpitou, their target for avenging Kite, awaits. Inside they find Doctor Blythe hovering over a gravely wounded Komugi. When Gon spots Pitou, he is surrounded by a cloud of vehement aura.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170288/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"フクシュウ×ト×シュウフク\"},{\"title\":\"Insult x and x Payback\",\"number\":117,\"airDate\":\"2014-02-19\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"After Zeno leaves the palace, he is stopped by Cheetu. Cheetu wants to test his new ability on Zeno. After Zeno warns Cheetu to watch his back, Cheetu is immediately attacked from behind. Meanwhile, Knuckle is carrying a gravely injured Shoot and trying to escape Youpi.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/105057/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ブジョク×ニハ×セツジョク\"},{\"title\":\"A x False x Rage\",\"number\":118,\"airDate\":\"2014-02-26\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Youpi pretends to grow increasingly irritated by Loanboy`s interest tick and lose his temper. At the same time, the disguised Ikalgo is searching the palace for Palm.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/105058/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"イツワリ×ノ×イカリ\"},{\"title\":\"Strong x or x Weak\",\"number\":119,\"airDate\":\"2014-03-05\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"As Youpi begins to respect the Hunters` abilities, Ikalgo is hiding underneath the truck that was blown up by Brovada.  As Ikalgo continues to search for Palm, he notices that the elevator is not moving after Brovada stepped in.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/105059/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ツヨ×イカ×ヨワ×イカ\"},{\"title\":\"Fake x and x Real\",\"number\":120,\"airDate\":\"2014-03-12\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Knuckle is very upset when he discovers that the gravely injured Shoot is missing.  Meanwhile, Morel ends his vigil outside Pouf`s cocoon and takes action.  He lifts his giant pipe and shatters the cocoon.  As expected, Pouf is not inside.  Pouf was standing outside above the throne room.  As Pouf laughed, Morel noticed that something seemed odd about Pouf.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/105060/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ニセモノ×ト×ホンモノ\"},{\"title\":\"Defeat x and x Dignity\",\"number\":121,\"airDate\":\"2014-03-19\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Neferpitou is occupied using Doctor Blythe to heal the injured Komugi. Gon waits nearby for the healing to finish. As Shaiapouf watches from the back of the room, he notices that something is wrong.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/105061/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ハイボク×ト×メンボク\"},{\"title\":\"Pose x and x Name\",\"number\":122,\"airDate\":\"2014-03-26\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Zeno`s Dragon Head flies through the night sky to deliver is cargo to the battlefield. The King, Mereum, stands on its arm. Netero stands on its body. Upon arrival, the King asks Netero why he wants to fight.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/105062/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"タテマエ×ト×ナマエ\"},{\"title\":\"Centipede x and x Memory\",\"number\":123,\"airDate\":\"2014-04-02\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"As the fight between the King and Chairman Netero begins, Ikalgo is still underground lamenting his inability to finish off Brovada. However, Ikalgo recalls his mission to find Palm and pulls himself together.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/105063/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ムカデ×ト×オモイデ\"},{\"title\":\"Breakdown x and x Awakening\",\"number\":124,\"airDate\":\"2014-04-09\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"After Killua finishes recharging, he races back to Gon. However, he stops when he notices that someone is watching him. As he stands in the quiet hallway, a woman with long hair walks towards him.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/105064/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ケッカイ×ト×カクセイ\"},{\"title\":\"Great Power x and x Ultimate Power\",\"number\":125,\"airDate\":\"2014-04-16\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Shaiapouf and Menthuthuyoupi rush to find the King. At the same time, Neferpitou continues to use Doctor Blythe to heal Komugi on the second floor of the palace while Gon sits nearby. Behind Gon stands Pouf, and behind Pouf is Knuckle, who ignored Melereon`s warnings and revealed himself to challenge Pouf to a duel.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/105065/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ブノツヨミ×ト×ブノキワミ\"},{\"title\":\"Zero x and x Rose\",\"number\":126,\"airDate\":\"2014-04-23\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Netero uses his ultimate technique, 100-Type Guanyin Bodhisattva, to repeatedly strike the King into the ground, as though he is swatting a fly around. However, the King is unscathed. The King attempts to counter Netero`s attacks while Netero mounts a defense, leading to an intricate melee.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/105066/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ゼロ×ト×ローズ\"},{\"title\":\"Hostility x and x Determination\",\"number\":127,\"airDate\":\"2014-04-30\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"\\\"Mereum. That`s your name.\\\" Netero finally tells the King his name. In the next moment, he is engulfed by blinding light. When Netero stopped his own heart, he triggered the powerful bomb inside his body named Miniature Rose. Netero self-destructed to put an end to the battle.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/105067/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"テキイ×ト×ケツイ\"},{\"title\":\"Unparalleled Joy x and x Unconditional Love\",\"number\":128,\"airDate\":\"2014-05-07\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Pouf and Youpi see King Meruem`s ravaged body. The sky is filled with their cries of anguish. Tears of despair streak down their cheeks. However, the King is still alive. Pouf immediately comes up with an idea to save the King. He tells the King to eat him. As Pouf sacrifices himself to save the King, his tears of despair become tears of elation. And in the end...\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/105068/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ムジョウノヨロコビ×ト×ムショウノアイ\"},{\"title\":\"Formidable Enemy x and x Clear Objective\",\"number\":129,\"airDate\":\"2014-05-14\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The resurrected King calls himself Meruem and appears to have lost some of his memories. With Shaiapouf and Menthuthuyoupi by his side, he returns to the palace to regain his memories. Pouf believes that as a Royal Guard who must carry out the will of the Queen, the King is better off not remember Komugi, so he sends his clones back to the palace to find Komugi and eliminate her. He soon comes across Killua standing on the wall of the palace with Komugi on his back.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170289/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ヒョウテキ×ト×モクテキ\"},{\"title\":\"Magic x of x Despair\",\"number\":130,\"airDate\":\"2014-05-21\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"King Meruem returns to the palace with Youpi and Pouf to find hundreds of thousands of humans lined up for the selection. Knuckle is hiding inside the crowd with Melereon waiting nearby while Palm stands by behind the palace and Ikalgo waits above the hallway. All of them grow tense as the King returns. Meanwhile, Pouf`s clones are searching for the Gungi board and pieces which will trigger the return of the King`s memories so he can hide them. At the same time, Gon and Pitou head to the hiding place in Peijing to heal Kite.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170290/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"マホウ×デ×ゼツボウ\"},{\"title\":\"Anger x and x Light\",\"number\":131,\"airDate\":\"2014-05-28\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon begs Pitou to heal Kite as tears streak down his face. Kite`s still body lies in front of Pitou. Pitou uses Doctor Blythe to heal himself instead of Pitou. After confirming that the fingers on his left hand move, Pitou tells Gon that he must kill him. Gon is shocked and calls Pitou a liar as he is surrounded by aura. A sudden gust then blows out the candles in the room...\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170291/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"イカリ×ト×ヒカリ\"},{\"title\":\"Flash x and x Start\",\"number\":132,\"airDate\":\"2014-06-04\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The battle between Gon and Pitou is over. At the same time, Meruem, Youpi, and Pouf stand before the west tower. Pouf is very worried that Meruem will remember Komugi.  As Meruem steps inside the west tower, he feels that something is missing.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170292/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"センコウ×ト×ハツドウ\"},{\"title\":\"Deadline x to x Live\",\"number\":133,\"airDate\":\"2014-06-11\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Pouf is worried that Meruem will remember Komugi.  However, he must carry out his duty and spread pollen to the remaining citizens, despite the decrease in his power after offering his own body to the King.  Pouf soon realizes that Pitou has not returned.  Pouf does not the resolution of the battle between Gon and Pitou.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170293/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"セイゾン×ノ×キゲン\"},{\"title\":\"The Word x Is x That Someone\",\"number\":134,\"airDate\":\"2014-06-18\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"King Meruem was able to recover from his near-death state after the Miniature Rose explosion.  However, he cannot remember Komugi.  At the same time, he realizes that Shaiapouf is hiding something from him.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170294/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ヒトコト×ハ× ソノヒト\"},{\"title\":\"This Person x and x This Moment\",\"number\":135,\"airDate\":\"2014-06-25\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"One word from Welfin is all it takes for Meruem to remember Komugi.  Having moved underground, the King transforms his aura into particles to find where Palm is hiding.  When the King declares that the battle is over and reveals his reason for coming to Palm, she is shocked.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170295/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"コノヒ×ト×コノシュンカン\"},{\"title\":\"Homecoming x and x True Name\",\"number\":136,\"airDate\":\"2014-07-02\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"With the death of King Meruem, the battle between humans and Chimera Ants comes to an end. The humans suffered great casualties, but they emerge victorious. Welfin, Brovada, Hina, Shidore, and the other Chimera Ants, some with memories of their previous lives and some without, choose to take different paths.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170296/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"キキョウ×ト×ホンミョウ\"},{\"title\":\"Debate x Among x Zodiacs\",\"number\":137,\"airDate\":\"2014-07-09\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The leaders of the Hunter Association, the Zodiacs, have assembled. Gon`s father Ging is one of the members. They discuss how they will carry out Netero`s will and hold an election, but vice chairman Pariston quickly derails the conversation. Will the Zodiacs be able to reach a consensus?\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170297/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ジュウニシン×デ×ギロン\"},{\"title\":\"Request x and x Wish\",\"number\":138,\"airDate\":\"2014-07-16\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The election for Chairman Netero`s successor has begun. Hunters line up at the headquarters to cast their vote. The rules require that 95% of the 661 member Hunters participate, or the vote must be reheld. There is much confusion as the first and second votes fail to meet the requirement.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170298/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"オネダリ×ト×オネガイ\"},{\"title\":\"Alluka x and x Something\",\"number\":139,\"airDate\":\"2014-07-23\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"While Killua is reunited with his sibling Alluka, his older brother Illumi is seeking assistance from Hisoka and telling him the family secret regarding Alluka`s power. This power has the potential to destroy the Zoldyck family. When three of Alluka`s requests are fulfilled, Alluka will grant a wish.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170299/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"アルカ×ト×ナニカ\"},{\"title\":\"Join Battle x and x Open Battle\",\"number\":140,\"airDate\":\"2014-07-30\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The Hunter Association expert is unable to dispel the Restraint and Vow made by Gon. Killua ignores his family`s objections and takes Alluka outside the house to save Gon. He is followed by multiple butlers, but Killua does not stop. Will Killua be able to bring Alluka to Gon and save him?\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170300/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"サンセン×ト×カイセン\"},{\"title\":\"Magician x and x Butler\",\"number\":141,\"airDate\":\"2014-08-06\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"In the Hunter Association headquarters, the fourth vote to elect a chairman has just ended. Pariston finishes in first, with Cheadle in second and Leorio in third. However, the requirements still are not met, so another vote must be held. The fifth vote will be a runoff with the top 16 vote-getters...\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170301/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"テジナシ×ト×シツジ\"},{\"title\":\"Needles x and x Debt\",\"number\":142,\"airDate\":\"2014-08-13\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"As Goto and the other butlers assist Killua, they encounter Hisoka, who is helping Illumi to kill Alluka. Killua carries Alluka and runs through the forest towards Parasta, but he is followed by a shadowy figure...who turns out to be the butler Tsubone. After Killua puts on a burst of speed to shake Tsubone, she calls her granddaughter Amane who is also a butler and tells her to cut them off. Will Killua be able to reach Gon?\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170302/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ハリ×ト×カリ\"},{\"title\":\"Sin x and x Claw\",\"number\":143,\"airDate\":\"2014-08-20\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"After the 5th vote for the 13th Hunter Association Chairman, it`s determined that there will be a run off among the top eight vote-getters. Meanwhile, Hisoka is killing Hunters from the Seirin Group who seek to capture one of the Needlemen and discovers a map which marks where Killua`s airship will land. Illumi has obtained the same map and is in hot pursuit while the butlers Tsubone and Amane are also following the airship.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170303/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ツミ×ト×ツメ\"},{\"title\":\"Approval x and x Coalition\",\"number\":144,\"airDate\":\"2014-08-27\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"After the 7th vote for the 13th Hunter Association Chairman, the remaining eight candidates are cut down to four for the next vote. After Ging`s cryptic comment that the outcome is that there is no outcome, Cheadle asks him how to defeat Pariston.  Ging`s response is that Pariston doesn`t want to win and doesn`t want to lose, which is what makes him strong. What does he mean?\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170304/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"ケッサイ×ト×カッサイ\"},{\"title\":\"Defeat x and x Reunion\",\"number\":145,\"airDate\":\"2014-09-03\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The election for chairman is now on its 8th vote. Beans releases the results of the vote which are displayed on the screen for everyone to see and there is quite a stir. The result is that Leorio is in 1st while Pariston is in 2nd. However, Leorio failed to secure 50% of the vote so there will be a final vote between the top two vote-getters. Meanwhile, back in Gon`s hospital, Alluka wakes up after napping on Killua`s lap. Killua makes his forbidden wish to Something.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170305/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"カンパイ×ト×サイカイ\"},{\"title\":\"Chairman x and x Release\",\"number\":146,\"airDate\":\"2014-09-10\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon`s recovery is celebrated by the Hunters assembled in the Association headquarters. And Gon finally meets his father Ging for the first time. The Ging from the photograph in Mito`s house. The Ging that Satotz, Razor, and Kite spoke of. That Ging is now waving at Gon. Gon runs over to speak to Ging.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170306/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"カイチョウ×ト×カイジョ\"},{\"title\":\"Salvation x and x Future\",\"number\":147,\"airDate\":\"2014-09-17\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"The Chimera Ant Koala confesses his sins to a redheaded girl. When Koala finishes his confession, the girl quietly begins to talk. Meanwhile, Gon has discovered that Kite is actually still alive and goes to see him. What will Gon say when they finally meet?\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170307/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"スクイ×ト×ミライ\"},{\"title\":\"Past x and x Future\",\"number\":148,\"airDate\":\"2014-09-24\",\"duration\":25,\"synopsis\":\"Gon climbs the world`s tallest tree, and at the top he finds his father, Ging, whom he`s been searching for all along. Gon wants to tell Ging all about his journey so far: about leaving his hometown of Whale Island to find him, about passing the rigorous Hunter Exam and becoming a Pro Hunter, and about all the precious friends he made along the way. Gon`s first experience spending time with Ging as father and son awaits him.\\nSource: crunchyroll\",\"thumbnail\":\"https://media.kitsu.app/episodes/thumbnails/170308/original.jpg\",\"titleJapanese\":\"コレマデ×ト×コレカラ\"}]","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":86400,"tags":[]}